(1537066, 201763, 23394, '<td valign="top">ok, you have two things going against you as far as the challenge goes:  photo quality and meeting the challenge.  i appreciate your entering, and hope you aren''t getting beaten up too badly.  however this winds up, and regardless of the comments you get, don''t take it personally.  if you want to do better, you can--as long as you keep trying!<br/> <br/>here''s a couple ideas.  if this is the only type of sporting activity you could get, you could have done better if you had the kids line up like they were getting ready to start a race.  also, if possible, you could have shot this from every side of the pool, to see which one would have the best lighting.  another thing to try while shooting at this time of day is to use your flash (it will help capture details washed out by the harsh light of the sun).  lastly, you might want to check out this <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=156130#1084676" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">thread</a> -- it has some really good tips about scoring higher.  good luck!</td>', 'ok, you have two things going against you as far as the challenge goes:  photo quality and meeting the challenge.  i appreciate your entering, and hope you aren''t getting beaten up too badly.  however this winds up, and regardless of the comments you get, don''t take it personally.  if you want to do better, you can--as long as you keep trying! here''s a couple ideas.  if this is the only type of sporting activity you could get, you could have done better if you had the kids line up like they were getting ready to start a race.  also, if possible, you could have shot this from every side of the pool, to see which one would have the best lighting.  another thing to try while shooting at this time of day is to use your flash (it will help capture details washed out by the harsh light of the sun).  lastly, you might want to check out this thread -- it has some really good tips about scoring higher.  good luck!', '2005-07-15 07:20:46.000000', NULL, 1),
