(1537137, 203119, 23394, '<td valign="top">great timing, nice capture.  i think, though, you could really benefit from putting 2-3 thousand dollars into equipment upgrades.  you are really asking a bit too much from that slow lens (f/4?)  you need f/2.8 if you want to get action like this razor sharp.  i just happen to know of a mint condition canon 300mm f/2.8L that normally retails for $3700 for about $2700--let me know if you''re interested...<br/> <br/>oh, i REALLY like this and hope it does well.  as for the challenge, you absolutely nailed it.  i probably would have scored this an 8, but i''m giving this a 10 just to help offset the rough voting that i''ve seen in this challenge.  good luck, hope to see this on the front page!  (and yes, baseball is the best sport!)</td>', 'great timing, nice capture.  i think, though, you could really benefit from putting 2-3 thousand dollars into equipment upgrades.  you are really asking a bit too much from that slow lens (f/4?)  you need f/2.8 if you want to get action like this razor sharp.  i just happen to know of a mint condition canon 300mm f/2.8L that normally retails for $3700 for about $2700--let me know if you''re interested... oh, i REALLY like this and hope it does well.  as for the challenge, you absolutely nailed it.  i probably would have scored this an 8, but i''m giving this a 10 just to help offset the rough voting that i''ve seen in this challenge.  good luck, hope to see this on the front page!  (and yes, baseball is the best sport!)', '2005-07-15 08:10:32.000000', NULL, 1),
