(1537918, 202371, 37409, '<td valign="top">Lacks focus</td>', 'Lacks focus', '2005-07-15 15:57:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537920, 201646, 37409, '<td valign="top">I would have like the foot in ball less blurred and the grass less in focus.</td>', 'I would have like the foot in ball less blurred and the grass less in focus.', '2005-07-15 15:57:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537923, 202643, 37409, '<td valign="top">Best chess shot so far. At least you give the feeling of action.</td>', 'Best chess shot so far. At least you give the feeling of action.', '2005-07-15 15:58:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537924, 201967, 37409, '<td valign="top">Cool concept. Not very sharp though. Looks out of focus.</td>', 'Cool concept. Not very sharp though. Looks out of focus.', '2005-07-15 15:59:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537926, 203114, 37409, '<td valign="top">Nice shot. Good DO. The B&amp;W works well</td>', 'Nice shot. Good DO. The B&W works well', '2005-07-15 16:00:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537927, 202665, 37409, '<td valign="top">I would have focus in more on the rider to get rid of the foreground as its distracting.</td>', 'I would have focus in more on the rider to get rid of the foreground as its distracting.', '2005-07-15 16:00:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537928, 201928, 37409, '<td valign="top">Good shot. Nice composition, DOF, colors.</td>', 'Good shot. Nice composition, DOF, colors.', '2005-07-15 16:01:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537929, 202717, 37409, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot.</td>', 'Lovely shot.', '2005-07-15 16:02:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537932, 203165, 37409, '<td valign="top">Cool shot. I live the sharp facial expressions you captured. Colors are nice as well as composition and DOF, fits the challenge.</td>', 'Cool shot. I live the sharp facial expressions you captured. Colors are nice as well as composition and DOF, fits the challenge.', '2005-07-15 16:03:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537933, 202637, 37409, '<td valign="top">That ball has seen some action</td>', 'That ball has seen some action', '2005-07-15 16:03:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537934, 203250, 37409, '<td valign="top">Would hev been cool if the ball was more sharp and in focus.</td>', 'Would hev been cool if the ball was more sharp and in focus.', '2005-07-15 16:04:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537935, 203181, 37409, '<td valign="top">OOF</td>', 'OOF', '2005-07-15 16:05:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537937, 203078, 37409, '<td valign="top">Great shot. I love the composition, and colors.</td>', 'Great shot. I love the composition, and colors.', '2005-07-15 16:05:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537939, 202686, 37409, '<td valign="top">I would have liked to have seen the ball right between his legs. I see what you were trying to do with capturing the ball''s shadow. Still nice shot.</td>', 'I would have liked to have seen the ball right between his legs. I see what you were trying to do with capturing the ball''s shadow. Still nice shot.', '2005-07-15 16:06:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537941, 202997, 37409, '<td valign="top">Ahh you had the same idea as me. Couldnt find any players in the park though ;) The shirts on the men seem to be overblown. If you could tone that down it would be a great shot.</td>', 'Ahh you had the same idea as me. Couldnt find any players in the park though ;) The shirts on the men seem to be overblown. If you could tone that down it would be a great shot.', '2005-07-15 16:08:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537942, 202731, 37409, '<td valign="top">Would have really been cool if it were in focus.</td>', 'Would have really been cool if it were in focus.', '2005-07-15 16:08:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537945, 202294, 4281, '<td valign="top">This is a very happy picture as such, e.g. we feel the joy in the kid''s face as he is running.<br/>However, I don''t connect this picture very much with sports - more with playfulness.<br/>Other than that it''s quite frustrating that the right foot is missing in the picture - a wider view would probably have been more optimal here - and to have such an overexposed sky. <br/>I would probably have used slight Shadow/highlight in Photoshop to bring out the detail in the kid''s pants.<br/>Sharpening is perhaps a bit too agressive as can especially be seen in the kid''s pants. <br/>I also think this picture would have been much nicer in black and white.<br/>Íslensk, geri ég ráð fyrir? ;)</td>', 'This is a very happy picture as such, e.g. we feel the joy in the kid''s face as he is running.However, I don''t connect this picture very much with sports - more with playfulness.Other than that it''s quite frustrating that the right foot is missing in the picture - a wider view would probably have been more optimal here - and to have such an overexposed sky. I would probably have used slight Shadow/highlight in Photoshop to bring out the detail in the kid''s pants.Sharpening is perhaps a bit too agressive as can especially be seen in the kid''s pants. I also think this picture would have been much nicer in black and white.Íslensk, geri ég ráð fyrir? ;)', '2005-07-15 16:08:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537950, 203171, 37409, '<td valign="top">Nice try. Not really a sport. Great color. I would have tried to take a shot without the other bike coming into the image on the right. Maybe gotten down lower and tried to get a angle shot to get more bike as well the the rider.</td>', 'Nice try. Not really a sport. Great color. I would have tried to take a shot without the other bike coming into the image on the right. Maybe gotten down lower and tried to get a angle shot to get more bike as well the the rider.', '2005-07-15 16:10:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537954, 202175, 15273, '<td valign="top">could be a good concept, but, looks over processed IMO</td>', 'could be a good concept, but, looks over processed IMO', '2005-07-15 16:12:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537959, 203274, 38812, '<td valign="top">Nice picture, but isn''t that a man? The dog looks like a horse :p<br/> <br/></td>', 'Nice picture, but isn''t that a man? The dog looks like a horse :p ', '2005-07-15 16:13:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537960, 202974, 37409, '<td valign="top">This is my 10 for the challenge. Awesome shot!</td>', 'This is my 10 for the challenge. Awesome shot!', '2005-07-15 16:14:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537963, 201363, 34836, '<td valign="top">I think a tighter crop would have been better.  Good action shot.</td>', 'I think a tighter crop would have been better.  Good action shot.', '2005-07-15 16:15:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537969, 201278, 34836, '<td valign="top">Good composition.  Great capturing of the moment.</td>', 'Good composition.  Great capturing of the moment.', '2005-07-15 16:17:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537975, 203209, 34836, '<td valign="top">Not much action, but I like the overall appeal of this photo.  Very good composition.  I also like how all the different colors seem to work together.  Nice photo.</td>', 'Not much action, but I like the overall appeal of this photo.  Very good composition.  I also like how all the different colors seem to work together.  Nice photo.', '2005-07-15 16:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537980, 201981, 34836, '<td valign="top">Gotta be tough being sponsored by a funeral home.  Best sponsor I ever had was an ice cream parlor.  Good photo.  The crop could have been a little better.  You cut off one person on the rump, and the other, well . . . we''ll just leave it alone.  I like the picture though. Nice job.</td>', 'Gotta be tough being sponsored by a funeral home.  Best sponsor I ever had was an ice cream parlor.  Good photo.  The crop could have been a little better.  You cut off one person on the rump, and the other, well . . . we''ll just leave it alone.  I like the picture though. Nice job.', '2005-07-15 16:26:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537982, 202951, 34836, '<td valign="top">One of the best I''ve seen so far.  I''m predicting a soccer shot in the top three.  You caught the action at the right point.  Good facial expressions on the players that you can see.  You should do well with this one.</td>', 'One of the best I''ve seen so far.  I''m predicting a soccer shot in the top three.  You caught the action at the right point.  Good facial expressions on the players that you can see.  You should do well with this one.', '2005-07-15 16:29:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537985, 202744, 21915, '<td valign="top">way too much colour for my taste</td>', 'way too much colour for my taste', '2005-07-15 16:30:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537987, 201529, 34836, '<td valign="top">Sand blasts are great photos.  IMO you just missed the optimal timing.  It would have looked better if you could have caught the ball above the trap with the sand chasing it.  Not a bad shot though.</td>', 'Sand blasts are great photos.  IMO you just missed the optimal timing.  It would have looked better if you could have caught the ball above the trap with the sand chasing it.  Not a bad shot though.', '2005-07-15 16:31:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537992, 203136, 34836, '<td valign="top">This is a tough one.  I''m not sure the B&amp;W works.  She looks like she is in a tar pit.  There isn''t enough contrast in the dark areas.  The rest of the photo is contrasted well though which helps a lot.  Good capture of the moment.</td>', 'This is a tough one.  I''m not sure the B&W works.  She looks like she is in a tar pit.  There isn''t enough contrast in the dark areas.  The rest of the photo is contrasted well though which helps a lot.  Good capture of the moment.', '2005-07-15 16:34:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1537999, 203283, 34836, '<td valign="top">I''m glad your subject is actually participating in the sport and it''s not just a snapshot of someone on a bike.  You almost nailed this one.  The white lines make a great frame, but the square picture makes it look like he''s going nowhere.  This would have been much better if you could have stretched out the front end and moved the biker back a little.  You need to give the impression that he has some place to go or someone to catch.</td>', 'I''m glad your subject is actually participating in the sport and it''s not just a snapshot of someone on a bike.  You almost nailed this one.  The white lines make a great frame, but the square picture makes it look like he''s going nowhere.  This would have been much better if you could have stretched out the front end and moved the biker back a little.  You need to give the impression that he has some place to go or someone to catch.', '2005-07-15 16:38:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1538004, 202681, 34836, '<td valign="top">Nice pic of a watch, but if you didn''t have time to enter, why bother.</td>', 'Nice pic of a watch, but if you didn''t have time to enter, why bother.', '2005-07-15 16:40:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1538009, 203156, 34836, '<td valign="top">Good photo, but not great.  The ball is hidden, and the players in the back are kind of pieces sticking out of the players in the front.  Nice color.  Nice action.</td>', 'Good photo, but not great.  The ball is hidden, and the players in the back are kind of pieces sticking out of the players in the front.  Nice color.  Nice action.', '2005-07-15 16:42:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1538013, 202660, 4281, '<td valign="top">It''s a nice moment though it''s a bit unfortunate that the focus is on the guy to the right.<br/>It is also extremely strange to have the left guy''s right shoe disappearing into the ground. <br/>I''m of the opinion that this picture would be more suited to B&amp;W than colour as it is somewhat monochrome already (e.g. the lighting is very flat and and the guy''s clothes are alls black and white).<br/>Regardless of whether the picture is in color or B&amp;W the contrast should be increased. The easiest way to do this would be to do an autolevel in Photoshop but a slight s-curve would also help tremendously - //www.outbackphoto.com/workshop/photoshop_corner/essay_17/essay.html</td>', 'It''s a nice moment though it''s a bit unfortunate that the focus is on the guy to the right.It is also extremely strange to have the left guy''s right shoe disappearing into the ground. I''m of the opinion that this picture would be more suited to B&W than colour as it is somewhat monochrome already (e.g. the lighting is very flat and and the guy''s clothes are alls black and white).Regardless of whether the picture is in color or B&W the contrast should be increased. The easiest way to do this would be to do an autolevel in Photoshop but a slight s-curve would also help tremendously - //www.outbackphoto.com/workshop/photoshop_corner/essay_17/essay.html', '2005-07-15 16:42:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1538019, 202359, 34836, '<td valign="top">This one suffered from not being able to see faces.  I think a more rectangular shot may have been better.  Right now it''s a square picture with two guys right in the middle.  Stretching it just a touch to the right or left would have taken advantage of the triangle shape you have between the fielder, the runner, and the bag.</td>', 'This one suffered from not being able to see faces.  I think a more rectangular shot may have been better.  Right now it''s a square picture with two guys right in the middle.  Stretching it just a touch to the right or left would have taken advantage of the triangle shape you have between the fielder, the runner, and the bag.', '2005-07-15 16:46:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1538022, 202727, 34836, '<td valign="top">Great composition.  You''ve caught the lead rider in perfect focus and blurred the back field just right.  This photo really works.</td>', 'Great composition.  You''ve caught the lead rider in perfect focus and blurred the back field just right.  This photo really works.', '2005-07-15 16:48:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1538031, 202847, 33732, '<td valign="top">Wow!  The angle leaves me suspended.</td>', 'Wow!  The angle leaves me suspended.', '2005-07-15 16:54:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1538034, 203119, 33732, '<td valign="top">Very effective.  Seems like an angle more to the front would help.  This was a good capture.</td>', 'Very effective.  Seems like an angle more to the front would help.  This was a good capture.', '2005-07-15 16:56:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1538035, 203253, 33732, '<td valign="top">Great capture.  The ball would have helped.  I don''t know if the catcher''s glove was needed.</td>', 'Great capture.  The ball would have helped.  I don''t know if the catcher''s glove was needed.', '2005-07-15 16:57:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1538038, 202194, 33732, '<td valign="top">The subject could have been larger with less background.</td>', 'The subject could have been larger with less background.', '2005-07-15 16:59:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1538039, 202427, 33732, '<td valign="top">Good action.  All this splashing is either stopped motion or blur.  Here I like the blur.</td>', 'Good action.  All this splashing is either stopped motion or blur.  Here I like the blur.', '2005-07-15 17:00:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1538045, 202046, 33732, '<td valign="top">Tender shot.  Looks like fun.  Makes you happy.  Good luck.</td>', 'Tender shot.  Looks like fun.  Makes you happy.  Good luck.', '2005-07-15 17:04:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1538049, 202685, 4281, '<td valign="top">Very nice! Most certainly one of the better picture in this challenge!<br/>While one could argue that silhouettes have been done to death here on dpc and in photography I still think it is quite tastefully done here and it doesn''t detract from the action in the picture.<br/> <br/>The composition is quite nice though I wonder if it would have looked better in a square framing where one could see more of the bottom and the top.<br/> <br/>However, the main fault I see with picture is that it is somewhat difficult to understand the action in this shot. I noticed earlier this year when photographing snowboarders that they find it essential in snowboarding-photographs to see the ground as to be able to determine how high the snowboarder is jumping and what trick he is doing. Naturally, being someone who doesn''t know much about snowboarding I very often failed to do so, much to their dismay. <br/>Anyway, I wouldn''t exactly call it a fault with this picture that you don''t see the water and therefore it''s difficult to determine how high the guy is jumping but it would probably have depicted the action slightly better that way.<br/> <br/>One could also argue that the apparant ''grainyness'' in the lower half of the picture is quite distracting. At least I most certainly think that many people will give you a lower score than otherwise. However, believe this isn''t exactly grain but instead it is the water droplets flying upwards. Am I right here?<br/> <br/>Well, enough of this. Job well done!</td>', 'Very nice! Most certainly one of the better picture in this challenge!While one could argue that silhouettes have been done to death here on dpc and in photography I still think it is quite tastefully done here and it doesn''t detract from the action in the picture. The composition is quite nice though I wonder if it would have looked better in a square framing where one could see more of the bottom and the top. However, the main fault I see with picture is that it is somewhat difficult to understand the action in this shot. I noticed earlier this year when photographing snowboarders that they find it essential in snowboarding-photographs to see the ground as to be able to determine how high the snowboarder is jumping and what trick he is doing. Naturally, being someone who doesn''t know much about snowboarding I very often failed to do so, much to their dismay. Anyway, I wouldn''t exactly call it a fault with this picture that you don''t see the water and therefore it''s difficult to determine how high the guy is jumping but it would probably have depicted the action slightly better that way. One could also argue that the apparant ''grainyness'' in the lower half of the picture is quite distracting. At least I most certainly think that many people will give you a lower score than otherwise. However, believe this isn''t exactly grain but instead it is the water droplets flying upwards. Am I right here? Well, enough of this. Job well done!', '2005-07-15 17:07:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1538053, 202801, 4281, '<td valign="top">I like this one. If one would want to nitpick it doesn''t really show the ''action'' of basketball but I''m certainly not going to give you a lower vote because of that.<br/>Anyway, the main fault with this picture is that the hand isn''t completely in the frame. I wouldn''t go as to say that this ruins the picture but it most certainly loses some impact because of it.<br/>Other than that I like the framing, the background is nice and bright and out of focus and gives a nice contrast to the darker elements; the ball, the hand and the clothes.<br/>I would probably try to bring out a little shadow detail in the pants, most likely by using shadow/highlight in Photoshop.</td>', 'I like this one. If one would want to nitpick it doesn''t really show the ''action'' of basketball but I''m certainly not going to give you a lower vote because of that.Anyway, the main fault with this picture is that the hand isn''t completely in the frame. I wouldn''t go as to say that this ruins the picture but it most certainly loses some impact because of it.Other than that I like the framing, the background is nice and bright and out of focus and gives a nice contrast to the darker elements; the ball, the hand and the clothes.I would probably try to bring out a little shadow detail in the pants, most likely by using shadow/highlight in Photoshop.', '2005-07-15 17:13:09.000000', NULL, 1),
