(1545646, 202294, 39850, '<td valign="top">2 - DMC - A very nice portrait but - that is not what you were challenged to do.  Running in your socks does not a ''sports action shot'' make.  Maybe there were no nearby ''sports action'' opportunities, I don''t know - does that mean you have to forego the challenge?  If there was absolutely nothing else you could have ''created'' to ''fit'' (find that very difficult to believe) - in my opinion, yes.<br/> <br/>edit: this picture has ''stuck'' with me so I am taking the liberty of adding it to my favorites.  I hope you enter a similar one in a ''innocence'' or ''carefree'' or ''childhood'' etc Challenge one day.  It is has a very ''pure'' and carefree feel to it that is endearing and unique.  Also, fyi, the ''Outing with Grandpa'' I thought was another ''special'' shot, as are others I have seen of yours, like Fraehulstur.  I like your style.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-15 09:24:39.</i></td>', '2 - DMC - A very nice portrait but - that is not what you were challenged to do.  Running in your socks does not a ''sports action shot'' make.  Maybe there were no nearby ''sports action'' opportunities, I don''t know - does that mean you have to forego the challenge?  If there was absolutely nothing else you could have ''created'' to ''fit'' (find that very difficult to believe) - in my opinion, yes. edit: this picture has ''stuck'' with me so I am taking the liberty of adding it to my favorites.  I hope you enter a similar one in a ''innocence'' or ''carefree'' or ''childhood'' etc Challenge one day.  It is has a very ''pure'' and carefree feel to it that is endearing and unique.  Also, fyi, the ''Outing with Grandpa'' I thought was another ''special'' shot, as are others I have seen of yours, like Fraehulstur.  I like your style.', '2005-07-19 06:45:02.000000', '2005-08-15 10:24:39.000000', 1),
