(1549570, 202739, 15052, '<td valign="top">I just wanna say that this shot and the number 4, all we need is the ball, by Andri, must be disqualified because they are made by the same author: you can easly see that they are the same teams and the same players in the same city in the same day.<br/> <br/>Great shot but not correct <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-07-20 09:19:32.</i></td>', 'I just wanna say that this shot and the number 4, all we need is the ball, by Andri, must be disqualified because they are made by the same author: you can easly see that they are the same teams and the same players in the same city in the same day. Great shot but not correct ', '2005-07-20 10:04:05.000000', '2005-07-20 10:19:32.000000', 0),
(1549576, 202789, 15052, '<td valign="top">I just wanna say that this shot and the number 2, Grass explosion!, by Larus, must be disqualified because they are made by the same author: you can easly see that they are the same teams and the same players in the same day.<br/> <br/>Nice shot but not correct<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-07-20 09:20:11.</i></td>', 'I just wanna say that this shot and the number 2, Grass explosion!, by Larus, must be disqualified because they are made by the same author: you can easly see that they are the same teams and the same players in the same day. Nice shot but not correct', '2005-07-20 10:05:29.000000', '2005-07-20 10:20:11.000000', 0),
(1549667, 203168, 38927, '<td valign="top">Fooey, I thought this would do better, I loved it!</td>', 'Fooey, I thought this would do better, I loved it!', '2005-07-20 10:33:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1549680, 202634, 2223, '<td valign="top">Congrats Doc! Great capture, I stared at this in awe!</td>', 'Congrats Doc! Great capture, I stared at this in awe!', '2005-07-20 10:36:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(1549695, 202739, 4281, '<td valign="top">To answer Andy, Larus and I did indeed go to the same soccer match and we stood right by each other when we took those two, admittedly, similar shots. <br/>It might seem strange that we submit such similar shots even though we went to the same game but I can assure you that this was not planned on our behalf as Larus and I did not know of each other submissions until after the voting had started. Quite a coincidence, eh? <br/>In addition, I might mention that it should be obvious to most people that my picture and Larus''s have a quite different look to them (colour etc.) and the background is very different which, to me at least, shows that they were taken from different vantage points and were processed with different methods. Perhaps it''s moot to explain this as the site council will undoubtedly see when they receive the original files that these two shots were taken on two different cameras.<br/> <br/>(As an aside a similar thing happened to me and another photographer in the ''Abandoned'' challenge where the entries in the 3rd and 4th place were of the same house.)<br/> <br/>I could also mention that Larus and I were not the only ones to submit photographs from this game as Sjonni and hrutsen also submitted a picture from this exact match. <br/>And to boot Arnit, Siggi and skarason also all submitted photographs from the same game.<br/> <br/>Anyway, congratulations for your red ribbon, Larus!!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-07-20 09:54:11.</i></td>', 'To answer Andy, Larus and I did indeed go to the same soccer match and we stood right by each other when we took those two, admittedly, similar shots. It might seem strange that we submit such similar shots even though we went to the same game but I can assure you that this was not planned on our behalf as Larus and I did not know of each other submissions until after the voting had started. Quite a coincidence, eh? In addition, I might mention that it should be obvious to most people that my picture and Larus''s have a quite different look to them (colour etc.) and the background is very different which, to me at least, shows that they were taken from different vantage points and were processed with different methods. Perhaps it''s moot to explain this as the site council will undoubtedly see when they receive the original files that these two shots were taken on two different cameras. (As an aside a similar thing happened to me and another photographer in the ''Abandoned'' challenge where the entries in the 3rd and 4th place were of the same house.) I could also mention that Larus and I were not the only ones to submit photographs from this game as Sjonni and hrutsen also submitted a picture from this exact match. And to boot Arnit, Siggi and skarason also all submitted photographs from the same game. Anyway, congratulations for your red ribbon, Larus!!', '2005-07-20 10:40:03.000000', '2005-07-20 10:54:11.000000', 0),
(1549702, 202634, 36437, '<td valign="top">Great job I didn''t give you a 1. I was doing the !!!! when I wrote also 1. Sorry for the mistake. I love this shot. :-)</td>', 'Great job I didn''t give you a 1. I was doing the !!!! when I wrote also 1. Sorry for the mistake. I love this shot. :-)', '2005-07-20 10:41:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1549826, 202870, 30817, '<td valign="top">To those who suggested cropping some off the bottom: visualize how that would diminish the impact from the big air displayed here. Any part off the bottom means the subject is that much closer to the ground in the eyes of a viewer.</td>', 'To those who suggested cropping some off the bottom: visualize how that would diminish the impact from the big air displayed here. Any part off the bottom means the subject is that much closer to the ground in the eyes of a viewer.', '2005-07-20 11:20:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1549827, 202939, 29827, '<td valign="top">Very nice, tried a similar shot to this for a road signs challenge, but my SB800 just wasn''t powerful enough to expose the bike properly.  Be interested to know what equipment you used....<br/> <br/>Jamie</td>', 'Very nice, tried a similar shot to this for a road signs challenge, but my SB800 just wasn''t powerful enough to expose the bike properly.  Be interested to know what equipment you used.... Jamie', '2005-07-20 11:20:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1549828, 202870, 38592, '<td valign="top">This was one of my favorites in the bunch.  Like others said this would make a perfect cover for a bike magazine and you should consider sending it in.</td>', 'This was one of my favorites in the bunch.  Like others said this would make a perfect cover for a bike magazine and you should consider sending it in.', '2005-07-20 11:20:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(1549834, 201857, 26733, '<td valign="top">Great capture of the action. I really like how the drops (splash) of water look.</td>', 'Great capture of the action. I really like how the drops (splash) of water look.', '2005-07-20 11:21:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1550176, 202209, 19746, '<td valign="top">Two South Africans on the front page!  Bet you that''s the first time THIS has happened at DPC.<br/> <br/>Nice work, mate, fantastic capture!<br/> <br/>Alex</td>', 'Two South Africans on the front page!  Bet you that''s the first time THIS has happened at DPC. Nice work, mate, fantastic capture! Alex', '2005-07-20 12:48:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1550226, 203196, 40386, '<td valign="top">I like this photo although even with it being lower level dressage it doesnt portray this discipline to me. Palominos are always best shot with good lighting because they have a beautiful golden glow when the light is right.  Because the side nearest the camera is in shadow it makes the image look a bit flat and this would also affect the focus.  I think the crop is fine but would have liked to see the horse a bit softer on the bit.</td>', 'I like this photo although even with it being lower level dressage it doesnt portray this discipline to me. Palominos are always best shot with good lighting because they have a beautiful golden glow when the light is right.  Because the side nearest the camera is in shadow it makes the image look a bit flat and this would also affect the focus.  I think the crop is fine but would have liked to see the horse a bit softer on the bit.', '2005-07-20 13:08:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1550305, 202739, 27482, '<td valign="top">Edit:  Wrote additional info in the "Photographers Comments" instead.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-07-20 12:57:40.</i></td>', 'Edit:  Wrote additional info in the "Photographers Comments" instead.', '2005-07-20 13:41:06.000000', '2005-07-20 13:57:40.000000', 0),
(1550546, 202870, 7291, '<td valign="top">Wow!  First entry, first ribbon.  Nice job!  Can you tell more about the lighting?  It''s lit very nicely and looks like a tough exposure.  You froze the action very nicely despite the low light.</td>', 'Wow!  First entry, first ribbon.  Nice job!  Can you tell more about the lighting?  It''s lit very nicely and looks like a tough exposure.  You froze the action very nicely despite the low light.', '2005-07-20 15:02:31.000000', NULL, 0);
